[ti:Day 23]

[00:00.00]flexible 例 We should stick to the principles and be flexible as well. 我们既要有原则性，也要灵活变 通。
[00:08.82]guarantee 例 The makers guarantee this special glass is unbreakable. 制造商保证这种特制玻璃不会打 碎。
[00:17.80]bootleg 例 The country's bootleg alcohol reportedly generated fabulous wealth every year. 据报 道，每年这个国家通过走私酒获取巨额财富。
[00:29.73]hint 例 The director threw out a hint regarding bonuses at the end of the year. 主管暗示了有 关年终奖的事。
[00:39.48]cripple 例 Critics say that would cripple an already beleaguered economy. 批评者称这将削弱已腹背 受敌的经济。
[00:49.09]belated 例 The French protest strikes led to a belated vote of the reform bill. 法国工人罢工事件致使改 革法案投票时间后延。
[00:59.00]behalf 例 On behalf of our staff, I express our sincere blessings to you. 我谨代表我们的员工，向您表 达我们真挚的祝福。
[01:08.13]antedate 例 The invoice should be antedated to January 1st. 应该将发票日期填早到1月1日。
[01:15.72]mistime 例 His behaviours at work mistimes him. 他在 工作中的行为十分不合时宜。
[01:21.76]shortlist 例 He was shortlisted as a candidate for sales manager. 他被列入了销售经理一职的候选人名 单。
[01:30.12]whereby 例 I have made a phone book whereby we can liaise with each other. 我制作了一份电话簿，以 便我们大家互相联络。
[01:39.26]attach 例 Please attach these labels to your hand luggage. 请把这些标签系在您的手提行李上。
[01:46.69]halve 例 These impacts could halve the costs of dealing with climate change by the end of 2050. 这些作用能够在2050年底前将应对气候变 化的费用减半。
[01:58.61]anticipate 例 Intervention itself is a sign of failure, a failure to anticipate the moment of crisis. 干预 本身就预示着失败——无法预期危机时刻的失 败。
[02:11.62]alarming 例 Internet addiction among the youngsters has increased to an alarming extent. 在年轻人 中，沉迷网络的现象已经发展到令人担忧的程 度。
[02:23.24]asset 例 The higher inflation might drive more people to buy riskier assets. 通货膨胀越严重， 就可能驱使越多的人购买风险更大的资产。
[02:32.99]benevolence 例 The government's policies of benevolence receive everyone's support. 政府的仁政得到了 大家的支持。
[02:44.30]burden 例 The adoption of this policy would relieve them of a tremendous burden. 这一政策的采用 将为他们缓解巨大的负担。
[02:54.52]handle 例 Unfortunately, nobody here knew how to handle a situation like this. 不幸的是，这儿没有 人知道该如何处理这种情况。
[03:04.58]broker 例 You can sign up for automatic savings with your bank and broker online. 你可以在网上和你 的银行以及经纪人签署自动储蓄协议。
[03:14.80]avenue 例 The government instruction is the main avenue that modern economic regions form. 政府导向是现代经济区域形成的主要途径。
[03:26.57]trait 例 China's huge market potential is undoubtedly the most attractive trait for many foreign firms. 对于许多外企而言，中国巨大的市 场潜力无疑是最具吸引力的特质。
[03:40.04]integral 例 Teams will start to approach customer interaction as an integral part of their development lifecycles. 团队将开始把客户交互 作为其开发周期的组成部分。
[03:55.06]challenge 例 These costs can be justified only by the nature of the challenge. 只有挑战本身才能证明 这些成本的必要性。
[04:04.97]coefficient 例 The institutional change is the coefficient result of exogenous variables and endogenous variables. 制度变迁的产生是外生变量和内生变量 共同作用的结果。
[04:20.31]disparate 例 The cultures of these two companies were so disparate that it is really hard for me to adapt to the new one. 这两家公司的文化迥异， 让我很难适应新公司的氛围。
[04:35.33]affirm 例 The applicant for the post affirms that all the information he provides is true and correct. 这个职位的申请人坚称他提供的所有信 息都真实准确。
[04:48.33]spontaneous 例 We must be soberly aware that government reform is a passive adjustment rather than a spontaneous action. 我们必须清醒地认识到政府 改革属于被动调整而非自发行为。
[05:03.97]ergonomically 例 All of the office furniture in our company is ergonomically designed. 本公司所有办公家具的 设计都符合人体工程学原理。
[05:15.28]ceiling 例 Earlier this year, he led negotiations on raising the debt ceiling. 今年早些时候，他还就 提高债务上限与人进行了谈判。
[05:25.34]hospitality 例 Their hospitality left a very good impression on the guests. 他们的好客给所有客人留下了很 好的印象。
[05:35.10]appoint 例 We will increase our turnover if you appoint us as your sole agent. 如果你方指定我们作为独 家代理，我们的成交额将会增加。
[05:44.86]pander 例 The boss is good at pandering to the old staff without alienating the new ones. 老板善于 在不疏远新员工的情况下迁就老员工。
[05:56.00]ensure 例 We ensure that you will get the best quality with the lowest price. 我们可以保证，你们会用 最低的价格买到最好的产品。
[06:05.61]entrust 例 He entrusted a big sum of money to our care. 他向我们托管了一大笔钱。
[06:12.26]expense 例 The expense budget varies with the project. 项目不同，经费预算也不同。
[06:19.23]gallery 例 The plan is to erect a seven-floor residential building that includes an art gallery. 计划是建造一座七层的居民楼，其中还包括一条 艺术长廊。
[06:31.62]underperform 例 If you keep on pushing through the work, you'll eventually lose your focus, start to underperform, make mistakes and feel stressed out all the time. 如果你只是一味地去 完成工作，你最终会丢失工作重心，并开始表现 不佳，出现错误，同时一直感觉压力很大。
[06:52.84]exemplify 例 Exemplifying is quite common to make an idea easily understood when explaining something at a meeting. 在会议上解释某件事情 时，为了便于理解，通常会使用例证法。
[07:07.86]coordinate 例 It is your job as the release manager to help coordinate those two projects. 作为一名 发布经理，帮助协调那两个项目是你的职责。
[07:19.32]nonverbal 例 Eye contact is a very important nonverbal means of communication. 目光接触是一种非常 重要的非语言交流方式。 family-run business 家族生意
[07:29.54]track 例 Born on the wrong side of the tracks, he owned a company through personal efforts and determination. 虽然出身贫寒，他凭借自身 努力和决心拥有了一家自己的公司。
[07:43.47]unfurl 例 They unfurled a giant white cloth on which passers-by were invited to write down their proposals. 他们展开一块巨大的白布，邀请路人 在上面写下自己的建议。
[07:57.25]emolument 例 Civil servants usually have liberal emolument and long holidays. 公务员通常享受 优厚的待遇和较长的假期。
[08:07.47]grant 例 You should grant the users access only to the resources that they require. 你应该仅授予 用户他们所需要的访问权限。
[08:18.00]dossier 例 He is appointed to be responsible for maintaining the registration dossier. 他被安排 负责维护公司注册档案。
[08:29.31]hinder 例 The reformers have been calling for a rollback of rules that hinder law enforcement. 改革家们一直在呼吁撤销妨碍执法的条令。
[08:41.39]writeoff 例 This bar chart shows the sales figures of clothing stores in 2012. 这个条状图展示了2012 年服装商店的销售数据。
[08:51.30]influx 例 Venice attracted a great influx of holiday visitors this summer. 今年夏天，威尼斯吸引了 大批来度假的游客。
[09:00.90]cement 例 His considerate arrangement contributed much to cementing the pleasant relationship between the two companies. 他的周到安排对巩 固两个公司间的良好关系起了很大作用。
